GNU Typist lessons
==================

The .typ files in this folder are the lessons of GNU Typist (gtypist),
https://www.gnu.org/software/gtypist/, unmodified, taken from
https://github.com/gnu-mirror-unofficial/gtypist (an unofficial mirror of
the Savannah repository) at commit bda1c9dca77ebea6294f72d7ed09abe30a62a09f,
lessons/.  demo.typ and tinydemo.typ, which demonstrate the script format
rather than teach typing, are left out.

Copyright (C) 1998-2003 Simon Baldwin; (C) 2003-2022 Michael Opdenacker,
Felix Natter, Dmitry Rutsky, Paul Goins, Tim Marston, Mihai Gătejescu and
the other GNU Typist contributors named in each file.  GNU General Public
License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version; every file
carries the full notice.

kt*.typ were converted by the GNU Typist project from the lessons of
KTouch (https://apps.kde.org/ktouch/), and ttde.typ from TippTrainer; each
file's header names its source and authors.

index.plist is HomeRow's: it gives each course a title, the language pack
it goes with and the keyboard layout it teaches.  To update the lessons,
copy the new .typ files over these, adjust index.plist, and run the tests:
HRTypScriptTests parses every course and fails on one that is broken.

"upstreamWarnings" in index.plist is the number of gotos in a file that
point at labels which do not exist (cs.typ: 2, ru.typ: 1).  They are
upstream's and harmless -- those branches are never reached from a menu --
but they are counted so that a new one does not slip in unnoticed.
